Here is the full academic audit of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` using the **testsmells.org 19-smell taxonomy**, with integration-test calibration applied (the class carries `[TestCategory("Integration")]`).

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — 1. Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic  
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 93)  
**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // branch A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // branch B
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means only one branch ever executes per run. If the type returned changes across environments or refactors, the test silently switches branches. You're testing one behavior *or* the other — never both.

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden coverage gap — one branch may *never* execute in CI, giving false confidence.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — 2. Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test  
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)  
**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // hard-coded 3-second pause

Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Problem:** This is a smell even in integration tests (per calibration rules). The 3-second wait is arbitrary — too short on a loaded CI agent means flaky failure; too long wastes 3 s on every run. The `3000` is also a magic constant.

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();

    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            return; // success — implicit pass
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }

    Assert.Fail("Notification was not sent within the expected timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Non-deterministic failures in CI; unnecessary 3 s added to every suite run.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — 3. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Unknown Test / Assertion-Free Test  
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)  
**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertions anywhere
}
```

**Problem:** This test passes as long as no exception is thrown. Silent data corruption, duplicate-key violations being swallowed, or rows simply not persisting would all be invisible. The name implies "runs without errors" but the test *cannot detect* errors that don't throw.

**Fix — assert the outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    const int count = 100;

    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(count, users.Count,
        "All bulk-inserted users should be retrievable.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage metrics look good but nothing is actually verified.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — 4. Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette  
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)  
**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// four assertions, zero failure messages
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions with no descriptive message. A CI failure log will show `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<...>` — but without a message, the engineer must open the file to understand *which property* failed and why.

**Fix — add failure messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip correctly.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip correctly.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive auto-increment ID.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower incident triage; developers must context-switch to the source file on every assertion failure.

---

## Smells Not Detected (Clean Patterns ✅)

| Smell (testsmells.org) | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite (`:memory:`) is a hermetic resource — no external dependency. |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods. Integration calibration would further lower severity. |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` in `ListUsers` and `10` in the concurrency test are self-documenting (items just added). |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `ToString()`-based comparisons. |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks in any test. |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method. Setup is appropriate. |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or `Skip` attributes. |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions. |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests target distinct behaviors despite sharing `Insert` for setup. |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` properly. |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is meaningful. |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` calls. |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions. |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB always available. |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All tests have executable code. |

Tests like `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are well-structured with clear arrange-act-assert flow.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| **1** | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | 5 min | Prevents false-pass — this test is *actively lying* about coverage. |
| **2** | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | 15 min | Eliminates a hidden coverage gap — one branch may never run. |
| **3** | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | 15 min | Eliminates flakiness source and saves 3 s per run. |
| **4** | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | 5 min | Quality-of-life for CI triage; low effort. |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have smells, 3 are high-severity. The good news: the other 4 tests are clean and well-structured. Fixing the 4 findings above (roughly 40 minutes of work) would bring this suite to a strong state.
